{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791045550,"nonce":"eXzg6JwwBRQbWmcYgsyuY2ZcRiI=","title":"Smaller wrong-answer causes from the round","message":"- Issue6376: `Reflect.field(\"foo\", \"indexOf\")` is null: runtime reflect.rs `haxe_reflect_field`'s\n  builtin_box branch answers only `length`.\n- Issue5039: `@:bypassAccessor x = x + 1` bypasses the getter on the right-hand side too: the HIR Meta\n  arm sets `bypass_accessors` on the whole expression and MIR ORs it into every subexpression; Haxe\n  consumes it on the first field access only.\n- Issue9177: a `@:structInit` literal of a class with an explicit constructor writes the fields\n  directly instead of calling `new(..)`, so omitted fields get type defaults.\n- Issue1497: classes added by `Context.defineType` keep their `macro` fields unregistered and\n  unstripped, so `Defined.test()` returns an Expr pointer.\n- TestCasts: a `Float-\u003eFloat` closure stored in Dynamic and assigned to `Int-\u003eFloat` is called with the\n  caller's ABI (`maybe_unbox_function_for_target`, dynamic_dispatch.rs), so 123 lands in an f64 slot;\n  and `new MyClass.CI1()` in a package never loads module `q.MyClass` (imports.rs\n  `extract_all_dependencies` prefixes only undotted deps).\n- Issue7209 follow-up: nullary enum singletons are now per (enum, tag); boxed enums created elsewhere by\n  the runtime with zero params must use `haxe_enum_nullary_cell` too.","files":null}]}